    "intro": "Broccoli covers several related crops rather than just the green heads sold in supermarkets. Summer and autumn crops are mostly calabrese, which forms a central green head followed by side shoots, while winter and spring crops are usually purple or white sprouting broccoli, grown for a long succession of small spears when other fresh greens are scarce. Garden broccoli may not look as blemish-free as shop-bought heads, and summer crops often need protection from caterpillars and pigeons, but the flavour and the long season make it well worth growing.",
