    "intro": "Celery is a moisture-loving crop grown for crisp, strongly flavoured stems, and it is much easier to enjoy than to grow beautifully. Traditional trench celery gives the best winter flavour and benefits from a touch of frost, but it demands deep preparation, regular watering and careful earthing-up to exclude light from the stems. Self-blanching celery is simpler because close planting and a dense canopy do much of the blanching work, although it is less hardy and usually best harvested before cold weather.",
